# Keep `skills/aktion/` in sync with the codebase

`skills/aktion/` is the **Agent Skill** that teaches an AI agent how to author
complete applications in Aktion. It replaced `coding-gen-skill.md`, a single
4,153-line hand-maintained file that drifted through two feature waves until
**11 of its 22 flagship worked examples no longer validated** — they taught props
that do not exist. If this skill drifts the same way, every agent consuming it
generates broken UI, silently.

The replacement is structured so that most of it *cannot* drift.

## Which half is which

**GENERATED — never hand-edit. `scripts/emit-skill.mjs` rewrites these:**

| Path | Derived from |
| --- | --- |
| `references/components/index.md` | `getComponentCatalog()` + `defaultLibrary.componentGroups` |
| `references/components/<group>.md` | the same, one file per group, including `group.notes` |
| `references/builtins.md` | `builtinCatalog` + `findBuiltinConfig()` |
| `references/namespaces.md` | `namespaceCatalog`, `factoryResourceCatalog`, `routeMembers`, `i18nResultMembers` |
| `references/themes.md` | `builtInThemes` + `builtInThemeFonts` |

**HAND-WRITTEN — the judgement the generator cannot produce:**

| Path | What it carries |
| --- | --- |
| `SKILL.md` | Frontmatter (trigger conditions), the ten rules, the workflow. |
| `references/layout.md` | Rich-layout principles: pattern-first composition, visual hierarchy, **density targets per page type**, theme-aware authoring, anti-patterns. The reason the skill exists. |
| `references/gotchas.md` | Traps the schema validator cannot catch. |
| `references/patterns.md` | Worked application patterns. |
| `references/language.md` | A compact authoring reference. |

## Two build-time gates protect it

`npm run build` runs `node scripts/emit-skill.mjs`, which **fails the build** if:

1. **A `` ```aktion `` example does not validate.** Every fenced block tagged
   `aktion` is run through `getDiagnostics(code, defaultLibrary)` and must produce
   zero errors AND zero warnings. A block tagged `aktion` is a promise that it is
   a complete, valid program — tag fragments as `js` instead.
2. **A hand-written count disagrees with the library** (e.g. `SKILL.md` says 282
   components when there are 281).
3. **A component is in the library but in no `componentGroup`** — it would be
   missing from the per-group reference entirely.

So: after changing the library, run `npm run build:skill`. If it passes, the
generated half is correct by construction.

## Before changing anything under `src/`

Read `references/layout.md` and `references/gotchas.md`. They state the authoring
rules an agent is expected to follow; a change that invalidates one of them needs
that file updated in the same commit.

## After (or while making) a code change

| If you change… | Then… |
| --- | --- |
| `src/library/components/*` or `src/library/index.ts` — add/remove/rename a component | Nothing by hand. Run `npm run build:skill`; the group reference and the catalogue index regenerate. Then check whether `references/layout.md`'s composition table should recommend the new component, and whether any `patterns.md` example should use it. |
| `componentGroups[].notes` in `src/library/index.ts` | Nothing by hand — the notes are emitted into the group file. This is the RIGHT place to put "reach for X, not Y" guidance: it flows into the skill, the system prompt, and nothing else has to know. |
| Add / remove / rename a `$`-builtin | Nothing by hand for `builtins.md`. Consider whether `SKILL.md`'s cheat-sheet-level rules or `references/language.md` should mention it. |
| A namespace member (`src/language/namespaces.ts`) | Nothing by hand. |
| `src/theme/index.ts` — a theme or token | Nothing by hand for `themes.md`. Update the theme-vibe table in `references/layout.md` if a theme was added or its character changed. |
| An authoring rule, a footgun, or a new lint | `references/gotchas.md` — and if the validator now catches it, say so, because the whole point of that file is what the validator *cannot* catch. |
| A component signature used by an example | Nothing by hand: the build gate will fail and tell you which example and which prop. Fix the example. |

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit anything under `references/components/`, or
  `references/builtins.md` / `namespaces.md` / `themes.md`. Change the source data
  or the generator.
- Don't hand-write a component list, prop table, builtin signature, or count
  anywhere in the skill. If you find yourself typing one, it belongs in the
  generator.
- Don't add an example you have not validated. Tag it `aktion` and let the build
  check it — that is cheaper than being wrong.
- Don't duplicate `README.md` (host-page integration) or `dist/system_prompt.txt`
  (the full generated language reference). The skill points at both. Its own value
  is the layout/density judgement and the gotchas.
